<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">May 12, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 74 of Operation Epic Fury</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-05-12T07:00:00Z</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v45.1</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      The diplomatic track is in open deadlock: Trump's "garbage" rejection of Iran's counter-proposal cut <span class="cite">F2</span> (memo signed by May 18) from 35% to 15%, while the hardening of public positions on both sides nudged <span class="cite">F3</span> (Iran formal rejection) to 28% — the gap between a collapsed deal and a formal walk-away is narrowing as the Trump-Xi Beijing summit (May 14–15) becomes the last plausible reset window before the May 18 horizon.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">7 active · 2 resolved today · last reasoned 2026-05-12</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM bucket: ≤72h — no active forecasts today (F1 and F5 resolved; F4 horizon May 15 = 4 days) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">Near-Term (≤72h)</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast in this horizon today. F1 (Iranian public response) resolved YES; F5 (Saudi airspace) resolved YES.</div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS bucket -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 Days</div>

      <!-- F2: US-Iran memo signed by May 18 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F2 · 2026-05-11-us-iran-memo-signed-by-may-18</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a written US-Iran framework memorandum (the 14-point document or named successor) be confirmed signed by both parties before EOD 2026-05-18?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">15%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">↓ −20pp from 35% (2026-05-11)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-05-18</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Trump called Iran's May 10 counter-proposal "garbage" and the ceasefire "on massive life support" (CNN, Bloomberg, Al Jazeera, Axios — May 11). Pezeshkian responded with "we will never bow" language (CNBC, Press TV). Both principals publicly at maximum incompatibility heading into May 14–15 Trump-Xi Beijing summit. Axios reported talks unlikely to progress until Trump meets Xi. A signed memo by May 18 requires Xi-brokered off-ramp plus full reversal of public positions within 72 hours of summit conclusion.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if named US and Iranian officials publicly confirm signing; OR document text published by Axios/Reuters/State Dept with both parties acknowledging authenticity. Verbal agreement does not count.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>≥2 named officials from each side, OR official document release by State Dept/Iranian FM/Pakistani FM. Reuters/AP/AFP/Axios acceptable when both sides quoted.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If memo signed but Iran disputes key terms within 72h: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. If signed by envoys without principal (Trump/Pezeshkian) confirmation by horizon: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Witkoff/Kushner Islamabad return with Iranian counterpart</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC Quds Force statement endorsing diplomatic track</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F3: Iran formally rejects by May 18 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F3 · 2026-05-11-iran-formally-rejects-by-may-18</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran formally and publicly reject the current MOU framework before EOD 2026-05-18?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">28%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-up">↑ +8pp from 20% (2026-05-11)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-05-18</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Pezeshkian's "never bow" statement (Press TV, CNBC, May 10-11) and Baghaei's "unreasonable demands" framing (Press TV, May 11) adopt a defensive-defiant register. Neither used formal rejection language (rad, mardud, rejected, refused) about the US framework — both defended Iran's own counter-proposal. Per ambiguity rule, counter-proposal posture = NOT rejection. Small increase (0.20→0.28) reflects elevated hardliner activation risk if Trump-Xi summit yields no off-ramp; Kayhan has not published explicit rejection-grade language and Mojtaba Khamenei has issued no written rejection statement.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Iran's Foreign Ministry, Pezeshkian, or Khamenei's office issues public statement using rejection language (rad, mardud, rejected, refused) about the 14-point framework specifically.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Direct attributed quote in IRNA, Press TV, Tasnim, or Reuters/AP/AFP. Statement must name the framework.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Counter-proposal with modifications = NOT rejection (resolve NO). Walk-away from talks without explicit rejection statement = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Kayhan rejection-grade editorial on framework</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Mojtaba written statement against framework</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F4: Second Beirut strike by May 15 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F4 · 2026-05-11-second-beirut-strike-by-may-15</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will IDF conduct a second airstrike on Beirut (within the Greater Beirut municipal area) before EOD 2026-05-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">38%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-up">↑ +8pp from 30% (2026-05-11)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-05-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">IDF conducted a week-long Golani Brigade ground raid beyond the Litani River with 100+ airstrikes in south Lebanon through May 12 (Times of Israel), establishing the most intense attack tempo since the April 16 truce per UNIFIL. Al Jazeera (May 11): "Israeli killings in Lebanon rise — is even the pretence of a ceasefire over?" However, Smotrich resumed coalition voting after a compromise on reservist compensation (Times of Israel) — the Smotrich-as-Beirut-pressure-driver indicator is CONTRADICTED. US-Israel-Lebanon talks scheduled May 14-15 in Washington (State Dept) create a 48-hour diplomatic inhibition window. No confirmed second Beirut governorate strike between May 7-12.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if any Israeli airstrike or named operation hits a location within Beirut governorate borders. Southern Lebanon strikes outside governorate do NOT count.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Lebanese Health Ministry or major wire confirming impact within Beirut governorate; OR IDF spokesperson naming Beirut as target.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Drone strike on Beirut outskirts (Mount Lebanon governorate) = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO unless IDF/Lebanese government explicitly describe as "Beirut strike." Intercepted strike with no impact = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-CONTRADICTED">Smotrich public threat to bolt over Iran-deal terms</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Hezbollah rocket fire &gt;20/day from south of Litani</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N1: Iran revised proposal post-Xi by May 20 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N1 · 2026-05-12-iran-revised-proposal-post-xi-by-may-20</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran issue a revised formal diplomatic proposal (distinct from the May 2 counter-proposal) addressing the US negotiating position within 5 days of the Trump-Xi Beijing summit (i.e., by EOD 2026-05-20)?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">30%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast (2026-05-12)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-05-20</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Initial seed. Trump-Xi summit scheduled May 14-15 in Beijing; Axios (May 11) reported talks unlikely to progress until that meeting. Araghchi visited Beijing May 6 and Chinese FM Wang Yi pressed Iran toward diplomatic resolution (CNBC). A revised Iranian proposal within 5 days of the summit is plausible if Xi delivers a firm message, but Iran's "never bow" posture and the nuclear-vs-Hormuz sequencing dispute make rapid concession unlikely. Replaces F1 (resolved YES) as the new near-horizon diplomatic tracking forecast.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IRNA, Press TV, or Tasnim reports a new written Iranian proposal or revised counter-proposal submitted via Pakistani, Omani, or Chinese channel after Trump-Xi summit concludes (after EOD 2026-05-15). Restatement of May 2 counter-proposal does not count.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IRNA, Press TV, or Tasnim direct reporting; OR Reuters/AP/AFP citing named Iranian, Pakistani, Omani, or Chinese officials confirming submission.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If Iran offers to resume talks without submitting written document: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. If Pakistani FM announces receipt without Iranian confirmation: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Chinese FM Wang Yi post-summit communique citing Iran talks</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Araghchi travels to Muscat or Islamabad post-May 15</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N2: Project Freedom convoys resumed by May 25 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N2 · 2026-05-12-project-freedom-convoy-resumed-by-may-25</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will CENTCOM resume Project Freedom Hormuz escort operations (at least 3 commercial vessel convoys through the strait under US naval escort) before EOD 2026-05-25?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">40%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast (2026-05-12)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-05-25</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Initial seed. Saudi Arabia and Kuwait restored US basing and airspace access May 7-8 (WSJ, Iran International), removing the logistical obstacle that paused Project Freedom. The single Maersk Alliance Fairfax transit on May 5 demonstrated operational feasibility. Resumption is now constrained by Iranian interdiction risk in the context of the May 11 diplomatic breakdown. Replaces F5 (resolved YES) as the operational Hormuz tracking forecast with a concrete activity threshold.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Pentagon or CENTCOM confirms ≥3 separate commercial vessel convoys transited the full Strait of Hormuz under US Navy escort before EOD 2026-05-25. Single-vessel transits count individually if confirmed by Pentagon/CENTCOM.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Pentagon spokesperson statement, CENTCOM press release, or Reuters/AP/AFP citing named US military official. Shipping company confirmation requires US military co-confirmation.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If escort convoy turns back before completing transit: NO for that convoy. If Iran fires on and US repels a convoy that completes transit: counts as YES for that convoy.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Pentagon announces Project Freedom restart</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Maersk or MSC confirms scheduled convoy slot with CENTCOM</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS bucket -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 Days</div>

