        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Hormuz transit traffic at ~5-6 vessels/day as of May 3-5 (JMIC Update 041), against pre-war baseline of 138/day. Lloyd's Market Association confirmed war-risk premiums at 1.5-3% as of May 6 (Albany Antree) — the 1.5% indicator threshold remains unmet. Trump's May 11 "garbage" rejection pushed Brent to $104.97-107.67 on May 11-12 (Fortune, Hart Energy), with markets re-pricing toward extended closure. The single Maersk Alliance Fairfax escort (May 5) has not been followed by convoy operations. Probability reduced from 0.45 to 0.35 on the combination of diplomatic breakdown and sustained premium elevation.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
